            <ArticleTitle>Expanding subintimal coronary dissection under a stent-covered arterial segment: serial intravascular ultrasound observations.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>308-11</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A patient with an angiographically unrecognized minor coronary dissection in a stent-covered coronary segment in which a type D spiral dissection extended submedially to the distal artery is described. This complication occurred 6 months after stent implantation and was ascribed to injury of the stented vessel wall during an intravascular ultrasound study.</AbstractText>
